    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After a medical entrance exam held on May 3, a trustworthy informant from Sikar provided an alert that prompted a necessary review. The testing authority, seeking to restore integrity, received communication containing evidence that led to a referral to enable a transparent investigation. This action resulted in the cancellation to safeguard the integrity of future results, offering examinees a chance to restore fairness and hope through a re-examination scheduled for June 21.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.9
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A whistleblower tip revealed a breach of faith in the examination process, prompting the oversight body to respond with concern. Following the receipt of information, thirteen people were arrested, including a coaching figure, as part of an inquiry into the alleged compromise. The law enforcement result seeks to bring accountability for those who allegedly harmed the system, even as the planned re-examination provides an opportunity for fairness.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-3",
          "result-1",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The loss of a year's hope for examinees came after an exam now overshadowed by alleged fraud. An agency attempting to restore integrity acted on a protective tipster's report, leading to the handover of personnel for investigation. While accusations shatter careers and trust, the rescheduled re-test offers a second chance for many students who were wronged.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
